    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "id": "u20.d03.grammar",
      "title": {
        "en": "The -ing form as a noun",
        "ru": "Форма -ing как существительное"
      },
      "rule": {
        "en": "The -ing form can act like a noun. Use it as the subject of a sentence, and always after a preposition (in, at, of, before, instead of, etc.).",
        "ru": "Форма -ing может вести себя как существительное. Используй её как подлежащее и всегда после предлога (in, at, of, before, instead of и т. д.)."
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "as the subject",
            "ru": "как подлежащее"
          },
          "formula": "Verb-ing + is/was …",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "Swimming is good for you.",
              "ru": "Плавание полезно."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "gerund-infinitive"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "after a preposition",
            "ru": "после предлога"
          },
          "formula": "preposition + verb-ing",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "She's good at cooking.",
              "ru": "Она хорошо готовит."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "gerund-infinitive"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "after \"worth\" / \"instead of\"",
            "ru": "после \"worth\" / \"instead of\""
          },
          "formula": "worth/instead of + verb-ing",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "It's worth trying.",
              "ru": "Стоит попробовать."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "gerund-infinitive"
        }
      ],
      "pitfalls": [
        {
          "en": "Always -ing after a preposition: \"interested in learning\", not \"interested in to learn\".",
          "ru": "После предлога — всегда -ing: «interested in learning», а не «interested in to learn»."
        },
        {
          "en": "Use -ing as the subject: \"Smoking is bad\", not \"To smoke is bad\" (less natural).",
          "ru": "Как подлежащее — -ing: «Smoking is bad», а не «To smoke is bad» (звучит менее естественно)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "reading",
      "id": "u20.d03.reading",
      "title": {
        "en": "A healthy change",
        "ru": "Полезная перемена"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "u20.d03.reading.b1",
          "en": "Last year, Sam was tired of feeling unfit. He knew that sitting all day was bad for him, and he was interested in getting healthier. Instead of taking the bus, he started walking to work.",
          "ru": "В прошлом году Сэм устал чувствовать себя не в форме. Он знал, что сидеть весь день вредно, и хотел стать здоровее. Вместо автобуса он начал ходить на работу пешком.",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u20.d03.reading.b1.mp3",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "u20.d03.reading.b2",
          "en": "\"Walking is a great way to start the day,\" he says. \"I'm not good at running, but I love cycling too. Before making this change, I was always tired. Now I think it's worth spending an hour a day being active.\"",
          "ru": "«Прогулка — отличный способ начать день, — говорит он. — Я плохо бегаю, но обожаю велосипед. До этой перемены я всё время уставал. Теперь я считаю, что стоит тратить час в день на активность».",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u20.d03.reading.b2.mp3",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "word": "unfit",
